  "text": "Recipe: Chickpea \"Tuna\" Pita Pockets\nCreator: Dr Sirisha Potluri\nCategory: Pita Pocket\nIngredients: 1 can chickpeas (16 oz), rinsed and drained, 2 Tbsp oil-free tahini (or sesame seed powder), 1 Tbsp unsweetened plant-based yogurt, 1 Tbsp maple syrup, date syrup, 1 Tbsp lemon juice, 1 tsp salt-free mustard, 2 Tbsp diced red onion, Salt, black pepper, chili pepper flakes, diced celery, capers, sunflower seeds, pickled jalapeños, Whole Wheat Pita Bread, spinach, various herbs & spices\nCooking methods: no-cook\nInstructions: Mash chickpeas with a fork or potato masher. Add the remaining ingredients. Mix well. Refrigerate for at least an hour before serving inside pita pockets made by slicing Whole Wheat Pita Bread (sold in Trader Joe's, for example) into halves.\nNotes: Whole Wheat Pita Bread sold in Trader Joe's. A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (Whole Wheat Pita Bread), BEANS (chickpeas), RAINBOW VEGGIES (red onion, celery, capers, pickled jalapeños), NUTS & SEEDS (tahini, sunflower seeds), LIME-LEMON-VINEGAR (lemon juice), SWEETENER (date syrup), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
